2 CONT (Kisti Ballolfsdatter)
2 CONT
2 CONT At age 16, Kjisti worked for the Rev. Ross in LeRoy.  He was from New England and he taught her to read and write from the same books that his children used.  As a result of this, she spoke good English but with many "yankee" expr
2 CONC essions, and even learned to bake pies in the New England style.  Later, she worked for several years for a family in Cresco, IA.  She is remembered as a small old lady who always wore a cap and apron, with a limp from a broken hi
2 CONC p.  She immigrated in 1860.
