1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/68935245/elgar-arnold-thune
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Lars Knuds. Thune (b.12/31/1865 in Norway) and Kari Endred. Boyum (b. 3/2/1963 in Norway)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Ruth Lenore Torgerson (1900-1990) Divorced
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT Beverly, Barbara, Lenore, Arnold & Robert
2 CONT
2 CONT Elgar Thune, originally from Albert Lea, MN was an outstanding athlete who earned his way through college (St. Olaf) on an athletic scholarship. He taught & coached at Fargo/Moorhead where his team took state championships. (Recor
2 CONC ds from Moorhead H.S.show he coached there 1924-1925 with a 5 win 3 loss record. He is listed as Coach Elgar "Cherry" Thune)
2 CONT
2 CONT The family moved out east where Elgar became a president of Prudential Insurance. They later moved to Chicago where Elgar ran another insurance company. (Elgar & his wife Ruth were divorced & Ruth raised their 5 children.)
2 CONT
2 CONT GRAVESTONE INSCRIPTION:
2 CONT
2 CONT ELGAR A. THUNE
2 CONT MINNESOTA
2 CONT PRIVATE
2 CONT STU ARMY TNG CORPS
2 CONT WORLD WAR I
2 CONT DECEMBER 8, 1898
2 CONT OCTOBER 5, 1960
