1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://digitalcommons.andrews.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1043&context=books
2 CONT
2 CONT THIRD GENERATION 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Jacobson 
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 Ole, the son of Jacob Guttormson (Berge) Bjøraaker (3) and Anna Olsdtr. Gram, was born on July 24, 1844 on the Bjøraaker farm in Lærdal Township, Sogn og Fjordane County, Norway. He emigrated with his parents on April 14, 1866.
2 CONC  Ole’s parents joined the Greenwood Church about 1868.    Ole was married on August 19, 1870 at his home in Greenwood to Kari Einarsdtr. Nelson. The witnesses were Gutorm Einarsen (Kari's brother-in-law; Ole’s first cousin) and An
2 CONC ders Johnson (Ole's brother-in-law) (Greenwood Church record).    Kari, the daughter of Einar Nelson Kvame and Guri Paalsdtr. Sprakehaugen, was born on August 1, 1850 in Lærdal Township, Sogn og Fjordane County, Norway.   Ole’s ne
2 CONC phew, Jacob Guttormson Hegg, married Kari’s younger sister, Johanna. Ole’s first cousin, Goodrich/Guttorm Erickson, married Kari’s older sister, Randi.  In 1874 and 1876, Ole used the name Ole Jacobsen Bjoragor. He also went by Ol
2 CONC e Jacobson, Sr. Ole Jacobson, 36, b. Norway, a farmer, is listed as head of household # 161/161 in the 1880 census for Greenwood Township, Vernon County, Wisconsin with his wife, Clara, 30, b. Norway, keeping house, sons, John, 8,
2 CONC  b. WI, Edward, 6, b. WI, daughters, Anna, 4, b. WI, Gerte, 4/12, b. Jan 1880 in WI, and mother, Annie Jacobson, 74, b. Norway, labors in house. The census was enumerated on June 21 & 22, 1880.  In 1896, they were farming 160 acre
2 CONC s (section 27, 80 acres; section 26, 80 acres). Ole Jacobson, 55, b. July 1844 in Norway, married 30 years, emig, 1866, a farmer, is listed as head of household # 204/205 in the 1900 census for Greenwood Township, Vernon County, W
