2 CONT
2 CONT June 7, 1934 The Wittenberg Enterprise Mrs. Randi Lysne Died Yesterday Mrs. Randi Lysne died yesterday morning, June 6, at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Sanford Iverson, in this village, at the age of 79 years, 10 months, and 21 
2 CONC days, after an illness of about a week. Funeral services are to be held 2:00 o'clock Saturday afternoon, June 9, at First Lutheran church, the Rev. T. Aug. Lillehei officiating. The pallbearers will be John Nessheim, A. B. Westlun
2 CONC d, A. A. Grimstad, Nels Jacobson, Peter Mathieson and Eric Hanson. Mrs. Lysne's obituary will appear in next week's issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT June 14, 1934 The Wittenberg Enterprise Obituary-Mrs. Randi Lysne Mrs. Randi Lysne passed away at the Shawano Municipal Hospital Wednesday morning, June 6, at 2:00 o'clock, following an operation. Funeral services were held Saturd
2 CONC ay afternoon at 2:00 o'clock from the home of her daughter, Mrs. S. P. Iverson, and at 2:15 at First Lutheran Church, Rev. Lillehie officiating. Mrs. R. G. Peterson sang, "Fly som en Fugl," and the choir sang, "Asleep in Jesus," b
2 CONC oth of which were beautifully rendered. The pallbearers were John Nessheim, Axel Westlund, Andrew Grimstad, Nels Jacobson, Peter Mattieson and Eric Hanson. The deceased was born August 15, 1854, at Lordagsoen, Norway, and was marr
2 CONC ied fifty-five years ago to Thomas Lysne, who died October 24, 1921. They came to America fifty years ago and two years later moved to Wittenberg-on a farm one mile west of Wittenberg. Surviving the deceased are three children: Ol
2 CONC e Lysne, address unknown, Mrs. James Bestul, of Rosholdt, and Mrs. S. P. Iverson, of this village; one sister in Norway, 13 grandchildren and 2 great-grandchildren. A son Oscar preceded her in death. Those from out of town in atte
2 CONC ndance at the funeral were Mrs. James Bestul and family, Mr. and Mrs. Martin Bestul and family and Mrs. Carl Auston of Rosholt, Halvor Woldum and Martin Woldum, of Decorah, Iowa, Mr. and Mrs. Hans Hanssen and daughter Eleanore, of
2 CONC  Winona, Minn., Mr. and Mrs. John Jenson, Mr. and Mrs. Boergen and daughter, Mr. and Mrs. Arthur Lien and children, of Iola, Mr. and Mrs. Del Moberg and Mrs. L. L. Larson, of Amhertst, and Julius Loberg, of Nelsonville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Halvor O. Woldum of Decorah, Iowa
