1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/244428802/david-arthur-lillquist
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT David Arthur Lillquist, 57, Phoenix, AZ passed away suddenly in his sleep June 8, 2019. He is survived by his father Arthur L. Lillquist, sister Karen (John) Filardo, and brother Keith (Judy) Lillquist. Beloved Sons Magnus and Hen
2 CONC ry Lillquist. Many aunts, uncles, cousins, nieces, nephews and friends. Also, colleagues from his professional career in the heavy equipment industry. He was currently National Accounts Manager Central Region for Skyjack Inc. He w
2 CONC as preceded in death by his mother Beverly and step-mother Neen.
2 CONT
2 CONT A private family service will be held to celebrate his life at Malvick Lutheran church officiated by Rev. Karin Moberg. Interment will be at Guthrie Cemetery. In lieu of flowers, memorials can be sent to donor's choice.
2 CONT
2 CONT From VertiKal.net:
2 CONT We have received the sad news that Skyjack national account manager David 'Dave' Arthur Lillquist, 57, passed away in his sleep on June 8th.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined Skyjack five years ago, from Ritchie Brothers and spent more than 20 years in the aerial lift rental business with United Rentals, Hertz and Ziegler Cat Rental store.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dave Lillquist
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by wife Amy, sons Magnus and Henrik, father Arthur, sister Karen and brother Keith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Skyjack said: "Those who knew Dave know that he was an honest and jovial man who loved to make people smile. He was also a very dear friend and co-worker although, with Dave's vibrant personality, working with him never did feel l
2 CONC ike a job. He was always professional, diligent, and above all honest and built relationships with colleagues and clients, which turned quite easily into friendships."
2 CONT
2 CONT A private family service will be held to celebrate his life at Malvick Lutheran church, with interment at Gurthrie Cemetery.
