1 NAME Paul Ellsworth Elsworth /Anderson/
2 GIVN Paul Ellsworth Elsworth
2 _MARNM Anderson
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Little Cedar Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Adams
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 MAY 1935
2 ADDR
3 CITY Adams
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 MAR 1969
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rochester
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/17233438/paul-ellsworth-anderson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Adams Township
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Adams Review, April 3, 1969:
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul Ellsworth Anderson was born May 5th, 1935 at Adams. He was baptized and confirmed at Little Cedar Lutheran Church. He attended school at Adams Public School.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 14th, 1952 he was married to Lenore Thune. Two children were born to them: Kim David and Laura Alice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those who survive him are his wife, Lenore, son Kim, and daughter, Laurie, his parents, Mr. and Mrs. Arnold Anderson; brother Willard of St. Paul, sister Ramona (Mrs. Robert Hanson) of Adams, nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT On March 19th Paul received critical head injuries in a car accident and was taken to St. Olaf Hospital at Austin. He was transferred to St. Mary's Hospital in Rochester where he stayed until the time of his death on March 24th.
2 CONT
2 CONT His life's work was farming. He has been active in many community and church affairs. he will be missed by those who knew him, especially his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT May God bless his memory.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Adams Review, March 27, 1969:
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul Anderson, 33, died Tuesday of head and chest injuries received in a one-car accident March 19th.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anderson was thrown from his car after it hit the right shoulder of the road and then went into the opposite ditch about 1-1/2 miles west of Rose Creek on Highway 56. He had been hospitalized at St. Mary's Hospital, Rochester. His
2 CONC  death is the first 1969 fatality in Mower County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at Little Cedar Lutheran Church, 1:30 PM, Thursday, Pastor Wayne Quibell officiating. Interment will be in Little Cedar Cemetery. Adams, Funeral Home is in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anderson is survived by his wife, one son and one daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was named Outstanding Young Farmer by the Austin Jaycees in 1967.
