0 @N6000000005564374162@ NOTE Prest, bl. skipsprest hos Tordenskjold. Sokneprest i Oddernes 1718. En kranglefant sier en av kildene. Barna Hans og Kirsten heldt pengekrangel gåande i årtier etter dette.
0 @N6000000005564367978@ NOTE Han var capit. des amres (våpenmester, underoffiser) fenrik i Vikske kompani, Sogn. Fofatter. Ugift
0 @N6000000005564374040@ NOTE Kapteinvaktmester Fredrikstad festning 1740
0 @N6000000005564367987@ NOTE Familien eide garden Øvre Vilberg i Sørum
0 @N6000000005564367769@ NOTE Skal ha studert jus, men tok ingen eksamen (Kjel T. Lund 1997). Åtte Øvre Stele og fra 1741 også Nedre. Han delte garden mellom sønene Ove, Lars og Trond. Helge kom til Kongslie.
0 @N6000000005441186781@ NOTE Sogneprest. Han virket på Ingøy, Finnmark fra 1745. Jens forlot dette kallet
0 @N6000000008355473784@ NOTE I remember staying with Grandpa and Grandma Wold at Harry's cabin on Lake Minnewaska.
1 CONT He would take us out fishing and as we left the dock the gulls would follow the boat, because they new he would feed them.  We would catch perch and Grandpa would put his large thumb down their throat, break their necks, and toss 
1 CONC them into the air for the gulls to enjoy for their breakfast.  He would fillet the fish and we kids would watch in amazement at how fast he worked!
1 CONT Often Grandma would go out fishing with him, and I remember the two of them leaving the dock at Harry's cabin...Grandma in the front of the boat with her straw hat, and Grandpa tending to the motor with his pipe in his mouth - a t
1 CONC rue Norsk picture!
0 @N6000000008355476232@ NOTE Engaged in Farming until 1947 when he started working on construction as a Brick Layer.  In 1951, he moved to Mound, Minnesota where he worked on general construction until he retired in 1970.  He moved backed to Dawson in 1976 an
1 CONC d entered the Johnson Memorial Home where he resided until his death in 1981.
1 CONT
1 CONT Areta Wold Comments:
1 CONT "He was a tall, slender man full of jokes, good spirits, and curiosity.  He liked his drinks, too, and loved to dance.  Usually he was laughing about something so he didn't take life too seriously...
1 CONT
1 CONT Gustava, his wife was a resourceful, dind person-once in her youth quite a beautiful lady.  As a girl she worked for a rich family in Stavanger, Norway.  She had a daughter Ingrid who remained in Norway with Ole's family, either h
1 CONC is mother or sister.  Gustava, nine years older than Ole, had a difficult time keeping up with her husband.  She was a very good manager, a fine cook and a resourceful fouse keeper...
1 CONT
1 CONT When little children came to see him, he would give them money.  One or two took advantage of that, I guess.  Whenever something good happened to Ole he would always say "The man upstairs is taking care of me and I than him."
